  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Systems Strengthening and HIV/AIDS Prevention, Care and Treatment under the President&apos;s Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief: Quality Improvement Capacity for Impact Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quality Improvement: Using performance measurement tools adapted to each site, the Quality Improvement Center, in conjunction with MOH, facilitates the process of data collection and reporting to improve quality in PEPFAR programs. This program funds human resources for health, quality improvement and other health system strengthening activities in countries hit hardest by HIV/AIDS through the President&apos;s Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief (PEPFAR). Objectives include: (1) Training and technical assistance to build and strengthen care programs and health systems, so that affected countries can maintain programs over time and deliver quality HIV/AIDS care; build infrastructures such as clinic monitoring, health information systems, and medical and nursing education. (2) Enhance models of medical, nursing and midwifery education. (3) Develop partnerships between experts in the U.S. and people and institutions overseas to build skills and prepare host countries so that they may better manage their own programs over the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
